# One versions file (#14, M1 standing rule): every pin the release watcher
# and the bump procedure touch — Multica, OpenCode, and the LiteLLM /
# socket-proxy image digests — in one place. (Base and database images —
# postgres, pgvector, node, alpine — are pinned directly in compose and the
# Dockerfiles; the README pin table lists them.) The compose interpolation
# defaults and the daemon-image ARG defaults MIRROR these values — a unit
# test (tools/checks/versions-file.test.ts,
# CI-enforced) fails the build on any disagreement, so README, compose, and
# image can never silently drift.
#
# Bumps are deliberate (CLAUDE.md pin discipline): the Multica release
# watcher (.github/workflows/multica-release-watcher.yml) opens a PR with the
# LICENSE diff for the human gate — nothing here ever auto-merges. LiteLLM
# and CLI pins move only by hand (D2/D3).
MULTICA_VERSION=v0.4.26
OPENCODE_VERSION=1.18.10
# LiteLLM v1.94.0; socket-proxy 0.3.0 — the digests' human-readable labels
LITELLM_IMAGE_DIGEST=sha256:528774743b9efc02ee4612e99a79810df91188689ff4e569d9bcc79216b1e906
SOCKET_PROXY_IMAGE_DIGEST=sha256:9e4b9e7517a6b660f2cc903a19b257b1852d5b3344794e3ea334ff00ae677ac2
